    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is Dependency Injection?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Dependency Injection is a design pattern where dependencies are provided to a class rather than created internally, promoting loose coupling and testability."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "DI inverts control of dependency creation. Dependencies are injected via constructor, property, or method. IoC containers manage object lifetimes and resolution."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Dependency Injection",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public class OrderService {\n    private readonly IOrderRepository _repository;\n    \n    // Constructor injection\n    public OrderService(IOrderRepository repository) {\n        _repository = repository;\n    }\n}\n\n// Registration\nservices.AddScoped<IOrderRepository, OrderRepository>();"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
